# The P1 acceptance tests load pinned reference values, and setuptools ships
# only .py files from tests/ by default. Without these two lines the sdist
# carries the tests but not what they read, and collection aborts -- so no test
# runs at all from the released archive, not just the P1 ones.
# The golden generator lives under tests/fixtures/, which is not a package, so
# setuptools does not pick up its .py by default. It ships because regenerating
# the pinned values is part of what makes the claim checkable by a third party.
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tests *.json
recursive-include tests *.npz

# The citation file and the changelog. A distribution that carries neither makes
# the DOI unreachable for anyone who has only the archive, and leaves a user no
# way to tell what changed between the version they have and any other.
include CITATION.cff
include CHANGELOG.md
